    "evidence": "A freeze/blacklist capability exists now on rUSD's live Tempo deployment: rUSD on Tempo is a TIP-20 protocol precompile at 0x20c0000000000000000000007f7ba549dd0251b9, and the TIP-20 standard ships every token with pause(), TIP-403 whitelist/blacklist transfer policies, and burnBlocked(). The token's DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE is actively held by Reservoir operations EOA 0xb7570e32ded63b25163369d5eb4d8e89e70e5602 (granted at creation via TIP20Factory, Tempo block 12113547), which can at any time activate a blacklist policy, pause all transfers, or burn blocked balances; at Tempo block 32485354 the token reads paused() = false and transferPolicyId() = 1 (always-allow), but the control surface is live. By contrast the canonical Ethereum token 0x09d4214c03d01f49544c0448dbe3a27f768f2b34 (verified Blockscout source 'Stablecoin', non-proxy, OpenZeppelin AccessControl + ERC20Burnable only) has no blacklist, pause, freeze, or arbitrary-burn path, its sole privileged function is MINTER-role mint, and every EVM sidechain deployment is verified vanilla LayerZero OFT v2 + Ownable with no freeze surface (Arbitrum RusdOft source re-verified 2026-07-30), while the Solana mint has freezeAuthority unset. The canonical supply therefore carries no freeze reach, but the tracked Tempo TIP-20 deployment carries a real admin-controlled freeze/blacklist surface, making the honest asset-level answer true.",
    "reviewer": "Kimi V9 gap-clearing re-review (access freeze, 2026-07-30)",
    "reviewedAt": "2026-07-30"
  },
